var BlocklyGamesMsg={"Games.name":"C'hoarioù Blockly","Games.ai":"AI Lab","Games.language":"Language","Games.theme":"Theme","Games.themeAuto":"Auto","Games.themeLight":"Light","Games.themeDark":"Dark","Games.install":"Install app","AI.brushGroup":"Label examples","AI.brushA":"Class A","AI.brushB":"Class B","AI.erase":"Erase","AI.k":"Neighbours (k)","AI.train":"Train","AI.test":"Test","AI.reset":"Reset examples","AI.canvasLabel":"Training data plot. Click to add examples.","AI.examples":"%1 / %2 examples","AI.notTested":"Accuracy: not tested","AI.accuracy":"Accuracy: %1%","AI.target":"Target: %1%","AI.fail":"Not enough accuracy. Add or erase examples, or try a different k.","AI.pass":"Level complete!","AI.finalPass":"All 15 levels complete!","AI.next":"Next level","AI.allGames":"All games","AI.maxPoints":"This level allows at most %1 examples. Erase one first.","AI.help1":"There are only 4 examples — not enough. Choose <b>Class A</b>, click 2–3 times on the left, then <b>Class B</b> and click 2–3 times on the right. Press <b>Train</b>, then <b>Test</b>.","AI.help2":"Six examples give a rough horizontal boundary. Blue A belongs below the line y = 0, orange B above it. Add 2–3 examples of each class near the boundary. With k = 1 the nearest example decides.","AI.help3":"Four diagonal examples leave gaps. Blue A belongs below the line x + y = 0, orange B above it. Add 3–4 points on both sides, spread across the plot.","AI.help4":"Two examples are labelled incorrectly: an orange triangle in the blue area and a blue circle in the orange area. Switch to <b>Erase</b> and remove them.","AI.help5":"The labels are noisy. With k = 1 the machine copies every mistake. Raise k to 5–7 so a majority of neighbours decides.","AI.help6":"Only 8 examples for a circle. Add points around the whole circle, especially where the machine is wrong.","AI.help7":"Class A is rare. Add 5–8 blue points on the left, otherwise the rare class barely affects the answer.","AI.help8":"XOR: the classes alternate. One neighbour memorises every corner; try k = 3 or 5 to smooth the boundary.","AI.help9":"A circle. With k = 1 the boundary follows every point; add examples around the circle and try k = 3–5.","AI.help10":"A ring. Both the inner and outer edges matter. Cover them with examples; too large k blurs the ring.","AI.help11":"Two moons. The boundary is curved and close to itself. Start with k = 3; add points at the ends if errors remain.","AI.help12":"A checkerboard. Small k follows the squares, large k blurs them. Compare k = 1, 3 and 5.","AI.help13":"A spiral. Add examples along both arms; k = 1 memorises noise, k = 3–5 generalises.","AI.help14":"Budget: at most 10 examples. Spread them along the diagonal; one or two points per class can beat ten random ones.","AI.help15":"Final: a noisy spiral. Find and erase wrong labels, add points in problem areas, then tune k.","AI.howTitle":"How does it work?","AI.howBody":"The machine does not know the rule. It only sees the examples you give it. To classify a new point it finds the k nearest examples and picks the class that appears most often among them.<ul><li>Blue circles are class A; orange triangles are class B.</li><li>The tinted area is what the machine predicts.</li><li>Red crosses after Test are mistakes.</li><li>Small k follows individual examples; large k smooths the boundary.</li></ul>The goal is to generalise to new points, not to memorise the test.","AI.kHelp":"Small k follows individual examples; large k smooths the boundary.","AI.legendGroup":"Legend","AI.legendA":"Class A","AI.legendB":"Class B","AI.legendRegion":"Machine prediction","AI.legendError":"Test error","AI.coachAdd":"Click the plot to add examples","AI.testInfo":"Wrong: %1 of %2. Red crosses show where the machine made a mistake."}
